@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il33-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il33-readings`
IMPORT `nii-il33-fixtures`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-a1-ages`
IMPORT `nii-s2a-residence`
IMPORT `ml-payment-gate`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests: the Maintenance (Assurance of Payment) Law's gate. Row IL-33. Every expected value was worked by hand
-- from the Hebrew (lines 27, 36, 39, 42, 52, 66-69, 73-83 of the Law's deposited text) before the run.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN judgment IS A BOOLEAN
      child    IS A BOOLEAN
      lives    IS A BOOLEAN
      onDay    IS A BOOLEAN
      months24 IS A BOOLEAN
      enforcing IS A BOOLEAN
      allowed  IS A BOOLEAN
      from     IS A DATE
      to       IS A MAYBE DATE
      request  IS A DATE
      amount   IS A NUMBER
      rate     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `The facts of a maintenance creditor`
`creditor facts: judgment` judgment `, child's judgment` child `, lives with debtor` lives `, debtor resident on the day` onDay `, debtor 24 of 48 months` months24 `, enforcing` enforcing `, regulations allow` allowed `, from` from `, to` to `, request` request `, amount` amount `, regulations' rate` rate MEANS
    `The facts of a maintenance creditor` WITH
        `a maintenance judgment was given in the person's favour`                                  IS judgment
        `a maintenance judgment was given in favour of the person's minor child in the person's keeping` IS child
        `lives with the debtor`                                                                    IS lives
        `a resident of Israel in the Area within section 378 of the Insurance Law`               IS FALSE
        `the debtor was an Israeli resident on the day of the judgment`                           IS onDay
        `the debtor was an Israeli resident for at least 24 of the 48 months before the day of the judgment` IS months24
        `is pursuing enforcement proceedings on the judgment`                                      IS enforcing
        `the Minister of Justice's regulations let payment continue despite enforcement, section 9(d)` IS allowed
        `the day from which the judgment orders maintenance`                                       IS from
        `the day to which the judgment orders maintenance, if it names one`                        IS to
        `the day the request for payment was submitted to the Institute`                           IS request
        `the monthly maintenance the judgment orders`                                              IS amount
        `the monthly rate the regulations fix, if they are given`                                  IS rate

-- The ordinary creditor: a judgment in her favour, not living with the debtor, the debtor resident on the day of
-- the judgment, not enforcing; maintenance from 1 January 2025 with no end; the request on 10 January 2026;
-- 2000 a month by the judgment, 1800 by the regulations.
ordinary MEANS `creditor facts: judgment` TRUE `, child's judgment` FALSE `, lives with debtor` FALSE `, debtor resident on the day` TRUE `, debtor 24 of 48 months` FALSE `, enforcing` FALSE `, regulations allow` FALSE `, from` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, to` NOTHING `, request` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, amount` 2000 `, regulations' rate` (JUST 1800)

GIVEN departures IS A NUMBER
      flag       IS A BOOLEAN
      cumulative IS A NUMBER
      inMonth    IS A NUMBER
      exempt     IS A BOOLEAN
      treated    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The absences of a maintenance creditor in a month`
`absences: departures` departures `, the month is a departure, return or wholly abroad:` flag `, days abroad in the year` cumulative `, days abroad in the month` inMonth `, exempt` exempt `, treated as abroad` treated MEANS
    `The absences of a maintenance creditor in a month` WITH
        `departures from Israel in the calendar year, up to and including the month`              IS departures
        `the month contains a departure after the third, a return after the third, or only days abroad` IS flag
        `days abroad in the calendar year, up to the end of the month`                            IS cumulative
        `days abroad in the month`                                                                IS inMonth
        `exempt under section 9A(c)`                                                               IS exempt
        `treated as outside Israel under section 9A(d)`                                           IS treated

noAbsence MEANS `absences: departures` 0 `, the month is a departure, return or wholly abroad:` FALSE `, days abroad in the year` 0 `, days abroad in the month` 0 `, exempt` FALSE `, treated as abroad` FALSE

-- The creditor: a woman born 1990, resident since birth.
dana MEANS `a person` "Dana" `born` (YMD 1990 1 1) `who is` `female` `with` (`a resident since` (YMD 1990 1 1)) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`
March MEANS YMD 2026 3 1

§ `Tests — section 1 (a creditor) and section 2(a) (the right to ask)`

#ASSERT `ML s 1 — a creditor:` ordinary
-- Living with the debtor: not a creditor. A parent not living with the debtor, with a judgment for the minor child
-- in her keeping (and none for herself): a creditor.
#ASSERT NOT `ML s 1 — a creditor:` (`creditor facts: judgment` TRUE `, child's judgment` FALSE `, lives with debtor` TRUE `, debtor resident on the day` TRUE `, debtor 24 of 48 months` FALSE `, enforcing` FALSE `, regulations allow` FALSE `, from` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, to` NOTHING `, request` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, amount` 2000 `, regulations' rate` (JUST 1800))
#ASSERT `ML s 1 — a creditor:` (`creditor facts: judgment` FALSE `, child's judgment` TRUE `, lives with debtor` FALSE `, debtor resident on the day` TRUE `, debtor 24 of 48 months` FALSE `, enforcing` FALSE `, regulations allow` FALSE `, from` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, to` NOTHING `, request` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, amount` 2000 `, regulations' rate` (JUST 1800))
#ASSERT NOT `ML s 1 — a creditor:` (`creditor facts: judgment` FALSE `, child's judgment` FALSE `, lives with debtor` FALSE `, debtor resident on the day` TRUE `, debtor 24 of 48 months` FALSE `, enforcing` FALSE `, regulations allow` FALSE `, from` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, to` NOTHING `, request` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, amount` 2000 `, regulations' rate` (JUST 1800))
-- s 2(a): the debtor was resident on the day of the judgment, or for 24 of the 48 months before: either.
#ASSERT `ML s 2 — entitled to ask for a monthly payment:` dana `with` ordinary `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT `ML s 2 — entitled to ask for a monthly payment:` dana `with` (`creditor facts: judgment` TRUE `, child's judgment` FALSE `, lives with debtor` FALSE `, debtor resident on the day` FALSE `, debtor 24 of 48 months` TRUE `, enforcing` FALSE `, regulations allow` FALSE `, from` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, to` NOTHING `, request` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, amount` 2000 `, regulations' rate` (JUST 1800)) `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT NOT `ML s 2 — entitled to ask for a monthly payment:` dana `with` (`creditor facts: judgment` TRUE `, child's judgment` FALSE `, lives with debtor` FALSE `, debtor resident on the day` FALSE `, debtor 24 of 48 months` FALSE `, enforcing` FALSE `, regulations allow` FALSE `, from` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, to` NOTHING `, request` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, amount` 2000 `, regulations' rate` (JUST 1800)) `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- The creditor must be a resident (s 2A): a visitor (B/2) living in Israel is not.
#ASSERT NOT `ML s 2 — entitled to ask for a monthly payment:` (`a person` "Visitor" `born` (YMD 1990 1 1) `who is` `female` `with` (`a person living in Israel under` `a visitor's visa and licence of type B/1, B/2, B/3 or B/4, under regulation 5 of the Entry Regulations`) `and` `the work of a person who does not work`) `with` ordinary `, on` March `, reading` `the readings this row takes`

§ `Tests — section 3: the lesser of the judgment and the regulations`

-- 1800 by the regulations, 2000 by the judgment: 1800. 2500 by the regulations: 2000.
#ASSERT `ML s 3 — the monthly payment rate:` ordinary EQUALS 1800
#ASSERT `ML s 3 — the monthly payment rate:` (`creditor facts: judgment` TRUE `, child's judgment` FALSE `, lives with debtor` FALSE `, debtor resident on the day` TRUE `, debtor 24 of 48 months` FALSE `, enforcing` FALSE `, regulations allow` FALSE `, from` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, to` NOTHING `, request` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, amount` 2000 `, regulations' rate` (JUST 2500)) EQUALS 2000
-- The regulations' rate not given: refused by name.
#ASSERT REFUSED `ML s 3 — the monthly payment rate:` (`creditor facts: judgment` TRUE `, child's judgment` FALSE `, lives with debtor` FALSE `, debtor resident on the day` TRUE `, debtor 24 of 48 months` FALSE `, enforcing` FALSE `, regulations allow` FALSE `, from` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, to` NOTHING `, request` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, amount` 2000 `, regulations' rate` NOTHING)

§ `Tests — section 6(a): the period`

-- Maintenance from 1 January 2025, request on 10 January 2026: payment back to the LATER of 1 January 2025 and
-- 10 January 2025 (a year before the request): 10 January 2025.
#ASSERT `ML s 6(a) — the first day payment can be made for:` ordinary EQUALS YMD 2025 1 10
-- Maintenance ordered only from 15 June 2025: the later of 15 June 2025 and 10 January 2025: 15 June 2025.
#ASSERT `ML s 6(a) — the first day payment can be made for:` (`creditor facts: judgment` TRUE `, child's judgment` FALSE `, lives with debtor` FALSE `, debtor resident on the day` TRUE `, debtor 24 of 48 months` FALSE `, enforcing` FALSE `, regulations allow` FALSE `, from` (YMD 2025 6 15) `, to` NOTHING `, request` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, amount` 2000 `, regulations' rate` (JUST 1800)) EQUALS YMD 2025 6 15
-- A month wholly before the first day, a month wholly after it, a month in which it falls.
#ASSERT NOT `ML s 6(a) — the month beginning` (YMD 2024 12 1) `is within the period of payment of` ordinary `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT `ML s 6(a) — the month beginning` (YMD 2025 2 1) `is within the period of payment of` ordinary `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT `ML s 6(a) — the month beginning` March `is within the period of payment of` ordinary `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- January 2025: 10 January is partway in the month: declined by default; each reading by name.
#ASSERT REFUSED `ML s 6(a) — the month beginning` (YMD 2025 1 1) `is within the period of payment of` ordinary `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT `ML s 6(a) — the month beginning` (YMD 2025 1 1) `is within the period of payment of` ordinary `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `a month in which the period of payment begins or ends partway` `read as` `a month in which the period begins or ends partway is paid in full`)
#ASSERT NOT `ML s 6(a) — the month beginning` (YMD 2025 1 1) `is within the period of payment of` ordinary `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `a month in which the period of payment begins or ends partway` `read as` `a month in which the period begins or ends partway is not paid`)
-- The end: maintenance to 20 June 2026. May 2026 wholly in; June 2026 ends partway; July 2026 wholly after.
-- Maintenance to 30 June 2026 (the last day): June is wholly in.
GIVEN end IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The facts of a maintenance creditor`
`the ordinary creditor, maintenance to` end MEANS
    `creditor facts: judgment` TRUE `, child's judgment` FALSE `, lives with debtor` FALSE `, debtor resident on the day` TRUE `, debtor 24 of 48 months` FALSE `, enforcing` FALSE `, regulations allow` FALSE `, from` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, to` (JUST end) `, request` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, amount` 2000 `, regulations' rate` (JUST 1800)
#ASSERT `ML s 6(a) — the month beginning` (YMD 2026 5 1) `is within the period of payment of` (`the ordinary creditor, maintenance to` (YMD 2026 6 20)) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT REFUSED `ML s 6(a) — the month beginning` (YMD 2026 6 1) `is within the period of payment of` (`the ordinary creditor, maintenance to` (YMD 2026 6 20)) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT NOT `ML s 6(a) — the month beginning` (YMD 2026 7 1) `is within the period of payment of` (`the ordinary creditor, maintenance to` (YMD 2026 6 20)) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT `ML s 6(a) — the month beginning` (YMD 2026 6 1) `is within the period of payment of` (`the ordinary creditor, maintenance to` (YMD 2026 6 30)) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`

§ `Tests — section 9: enforcement`

#ASSERT NOT `ML s 9 — barred by pursuing enforcement:` ordinary
#ASSERT `ML s 9 — barred by pursuing enforcement:` (`creditor facts: judgment` TRUE `, child's judgment` FALSE `, lives with debtor` FALSE `, debtor resident on the day` TRUE `, debtor 24 of 48 months` FALSE `, enforcing` TRUE `, regulations allow` FALSE `, from` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, to` NOTHING `, request` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, amount` 2000 `, regulations' rate` (JUST 1800))
#ASSERT NOT `ML s 9 — barred by pursuing enforcement:` (`creditor facts: judgment` TRUE `, child's judgment` FALSE `, lives with debtor` FALSE `, debtor resident on the day` TRUE `, debtor 24 of 48 months` FALSE `, enforcing` TRUE `, regulations allow` TRUE `, from` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, to` NOTHING `, request` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, amount` 2000 `, regulations' rate` (JUST 1800))

§ `Tests — section 9A: absence abroad`

-- (b)(1) four departures: the month of a departure after the third, a return after the third, or a month wholly
-- abroad: nothing. A month that is none of those: paid.
#ASSERT `ML s 9A — not paid for the month because of absence abroad:` (`absences: departures` 4 `, the month is a departure, return or wholly abroad:` TRUE `, days abroad in the year` 30 `, days abroad in the month` 10 `, exempt` FALSE `, treated as abroad` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `ML s 9A — not paid for the month because of absence abroad:` (`absences: departures` 4 `, the month is a departure, return or wholly abroad:` FALSE `, days abroad in the year` 30 `, days abroad in the month` 0 `, exempt` FALSE `, treated as abroad` FALSE)
-- (b)(2) fewer than four departures and more than 72 days abroad in the year: nothing for a month with days abroad.
#ASSERT `ML s 9A — not paid for the month because of absence abroad:` (`absences: departures` 3 `, the month is a departure, return or wholly abroad:` FALSE `, days abroad in the year` 73 `, days abroad in the month` 5 `, exempt` FALSE `, treated as abroad` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `ML s 9A — not paid for the month because of absence abroad:` (`absences: departures` 3 `, the month is a departure, return or wholly abroad:` FALSE `, days abroad in the year` 72 `, days abroad in the month` 5 `, exempt` FALSE `, treated as abroad` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `ML s 9A — not paid for the month because of absence abroad:` (`absences: departures` 3 `, the month is a departure, return or wholly abroad:` FALSE `, days abroad in the year` 100 `, days abroad in the month` 0 `, exempt` FALSE `, treated as abroad` FALSE)
-- (d): treated as outside Israel.
#ASSERT `ML s 9A — not paid for the month because of absence abroad:` (`absences: departures` 1 `, the month is a departure, return or wholly abroad:` FALSE `, days abroad in the year` 10 `, days abroad in the month` 0 `, exempt` FALSE `, treated as abroad` TRUE)
-- (c): an exempt creditor is paid on the Minister of Justice's rules, which are not deposited.
#ASSERT REFUSED `ML s 9A — not paid for the month because of absence abroad:` (`absences: departures` 4 `, the month is a departure, return or wholly abroad:` TRUE `, days abroad in the year` 30 `, days abroad in the month` 10 `, exempt` TRUE `, treated as abroad` FALSE)

§ `Tests — a monthly payment is made for the month`

#ASSERT `ML — a monthly payment is made for the month beginning` March `to` dana `with` ordinary `and` noAbsence `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- Not a creditor (living with the debtor): none.
#ASSERT NOT `ML — a monthly payment is made for the month beginning` March `to` dana `with` (`creditor facts: judgment` TRUE `, child's judgment` FALSE `, lives with debtor` TRUE `, debtor resident on the day` TRUE `, debtor 24 of 48 months` FALSE `, enforcing` FALSE `, regulations allow` FALSE `, from` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, to` NOTHING `, request` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, amount` 2000 `, regulations' rate` (JUST 1800)) `and` noAbsence `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- Enforcement: none.
#ASSERT NOT `ML — a monthly payment is made for the month beginning` March `to` dana `with` (`creditor facts: judgment` TRUE `, child's judgment` FALSE `, lives with debtor` FALSE `, debtor resident on the day` TRUE `, debtor 24 of 48 months` FALSE `, enforcing` TRUE `, regulations allow` FALSE `, from` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, to` NOTHING `, request` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, amount` 2000 `, regulations' rate` (JUST 1800)) `and` noAbsence `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- Four departures, a departure month: none.
#ASSERT NOT `ML — a monthly payment is made for the month beginning` March `to` dana `with` ordinary `and` (`absences: departures` 4 `, the month is a departure, return or wholly abroad:` TRUE `, days abroad in the year` 30 `, days abroad in the month` 10 `, exempt` FALSE `, treated as abroad` FALSE) `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
-- A month before the period: none.
#ASSERT NOT `ML — a monthly payment is made for the month beginning` (YMD 2024 12 1) `to` dana `with` ordinary `and` noAbsence `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
